    "title": "University of Iowa Student Arrested After Flipping TPUSA Table on Campus - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Writer ,\n1 hours ago IOWA CITY, Iowa — A University of Iowa student was arrested Wednesday afternoon after allegedly flipping over a Turning Point USA (TPUSA) display table during a campus event, according to Johnson County Jail records.\nAuthorities identified the suspect as 19-year-old Justin Pham Calhoon , who was booked into the Johnson County Jail around 5:50 p.m. on November 5, 2025 .\nCalhoon faces multiple charges, including Disorderly Conduct – Disturbing a Lawful Assembly or Meeting , Criminal Mischief 5th Degree , and Harassment 3rd Degree .\nSee all regional updates on our Southeast Iowa News hub .\nThe incident reportedly occurred at a Turning Point USA outreach table on the University of Iowa campus. Witnesses say tensions escalated after a brief verbal exchange, culminating in Calhoon allegedly flipping the table and shouting at TPUSA members.\nHe is being held pending further proceedings. No bond information was immediately available.\nAccording to Iowa court records, Calhoon has no prior criminal history aside from a 2024 traffic violation in Ankeny for Failing to Yield Upon Entering a Through Highway .\nThe Iowa City Police Department and University of Iowa Department of Public Safety are investigating.\nNo injuries were reported, and no additional arrests have been announced.\nThe incident remains under investigation.\nAll suspects are presumed innocent until proven guilty.\nIowa News The post University of Iowa Student Arrested After Flipping TPUSA Table on Campus appeared first on Iowa Pulse .",
